<title>UK: Lloyd's of London chairman becomes Sir David.</title>
<headline>Lloyd's of London chairman becomes Sir David.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lloyds of London chairman David Rowland was given a knighthood on Tuesday in Britain's New Year's Honours list.</p>
<p>Rowland said his knighthood recognised the efforts of &quot;many, many people&quot; to complete the reconstruction of the Lloyd's insurance market.</p>
<p>Peter Davies, chief executive of Prudential Corp Plc, Britain's biggest life insurer, also received a knighthood.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Insurance News 44 171 542 2769</p>
